# THE SIFREI ROWS OF PISKAOT 153-156 (THE DEUTERONOMY WALK sitting 15 — CHAPTERS 17-18, LEAN, 2026-09-24): the court at Yavneh, priests and Levites in the court
# and a court without them, the judge of your own days, the details of judgment (153); death for the great court's ruling and not Yavneh's, for words of Torah
# and not of the scribes, the positive and the negative, right that is left (154); the rebel who acts, presumptuously, from the court's own mouth, the priest
# standing, the judge, strangulation, the three exclusions, the doers purged (155); the entry's reward, the king an insult and a commandment, like the nations
# (156). Every row READ WHOLE in both files; the cuts by ch17_ink.SP_. Sitting 14's form.
from ch17_ink import *
S = {}
def srow(p, r, verdict, prose): S[(p, r)] = (verdict, prose)

srow(153, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL COME" (17:9) — TO INCLUDE THE COURT AT YAVNEH. The head row of piska 153 ({SP_(153, 1, "לרבות", "בית", "דין", "שביבנה")} "to include the court at Yavneh"): THE HIGH COURT NOT BOUND TO THE PLACE — Yavneh\'s court after the destruction included by "come" (154:1 will take its capital power away): the compile\'s high court an office that survives the place\'s loss, an era-conditioned seat. Fresh.')
srow(153, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO THE PRIESTS THE LEVITES" — A COMMANDMENT THAT THE COURT HAVE PRIESTS AND LEVITES IN IT. ({SP_(153, 2, "מצוה", "בבית", "דין", "שיהיו", "בו", "כהנים", "ולוים")} "a commandment on the court that there be priests and Levites in it"): the court\'s composition a duty — the phrase\'s three book seats (17:9, 17:18, 24:8, asserted): the compile\'s court parameter. Fresh.')
srow(153, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'MIGHT IT BE A COMMANDMENT SUCH THAT WITHOUT THEM IT IS INVALID? "AND TO THE JUDGE" — EVEN WITHOUT PRIESTS AND LEVITES IT IS VALID. ({SP_(153, 3, "אף", "על", "פי", "שאין", "בו", "כהנים", "ולוים", "כשר")} "even though there are no priests and Levites in it, it is valid"): the duty not a condition of validity — "or to the judge" the saving clause (155:6 repeats it): the compile\'s court valid without its priests, the duty a separate flag. Fresh.')
srow(153, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHO SHALL BE IN THOSE DAYS" — R. YOSE THE GALILEAN: WOULD YOU GO TO A JUDGE NOT IN YOUR DAYS? RATHER, A JUDGE FIT AND ESTABLISHED IN THOSE DAYS; WAS A KINSMAN AND BECAME DISTANT — FIT; AND ECCLESIASTES 7:10 "SAY NOT THE FORMER DAYS WERE BETTER". ({SP_(153, 4, "שופט", "שאינו", "בימיך")} "a judge who is not in your days"; {SP_(153, 4, "היה", "קרוב", "ונתרחק", "כשר")} "was a kinsman and became distant — fit"): "IN THOSE DAYS" A RULE OF THE PRESENT JUDGE (the clause\'s three seats 17:9, 19:17, 26:3, asserted) — the judge of one\'s own generation authoritative, the kinsman-turned-stranger fit (Tosefta Rosh Hashanah 2:3): the compile\'s judge a function of the tape\'s day, never a past one. Fresh.')
srow(153, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL INQUIRE AND THEY SHALL TELL YOU THE WORD OF JUDGMENT" — THESE ARE THE DETAILS OF JUDGMENT. ({SP_(153, 5, "אלו", "דקדוקי", "משפט")} "these are the details of judgment"): the court\'s answer the fine points — the compile\'s ruling a structured value, not a verdict alone. Fresh.')
srow(154, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL DO ACCORDING TO THE WORD" (17:10) — FOR THE RULING OF THE GREAT COURT IN JERUSALEM THEY ARE LIABLE TO DEATH; NOT FOR THE RULING OF THE COURT AT YAVNEH. The head row of piska 154 ({SP_(154, 1, "על", "הורית", "בית", "דין", "הגדול", "שבירושלם", "חיבים", "מיתה")} "for the ruling of the great court in Jerusalem they are liable to death"; {SP_(154, 1, "שביבנה")} "at Yavneh"): THE REBEL\'S DEATH BOUND TO THE PLACE (Sanhedrin 11:4 the sheet) though the court itself is not (153:1) — an era-split effect: the compile\'s rebel-elder cell with the place as a condition. Fresh.')
srow(154, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"ACCORDING TO THE LAW THEY TEACH YOU" (17:11) — FOR WORDS OF TORAH THEY ARE LIABLE TO DEATH, NOT FOR WORDS OF THE SCRIBES. ({SP_(154, 2, "על", "דברי", "תורה", "חיבים", "מיתה")} "for words of Torah they are liable to death"; {SP_(154, 2, "על", "דברי", "סופרים")} "for words of the scribes"): the death penalty for defying a TORAH ruling, not a scribal one (Sanhedrin 11:3 the disputed sheet) — the compile\'s two classes of ruling. Fresh.')
srow(154, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND ACCORDING TO THE JUDGMENT THEY SAY TO YOU, YOU SHALL DO" — A POSITIVE COMMANDMENT. ({SP_(154, 3, "מצות", "עשה")} "a positive commandment"): the obedience a positive command. Fresh.')
srow(154, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"YOU SHALL NOT TURN FROM THE LAW THEY TELL YOU" — A NEGATIVE COMMANDMENT. ({SP_(154, 4, "מצות", "לא", "תעשה")} "a negative commandment"): the same obedience a prohibition — the pair the compile\'s two effects (an obligation and a bar) on one act. Fresh.')
srow(154, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"RIGHT OR LEFT" — EVEN IF THEY SHOW YOU THAT RIGHT IS LEFT AND LEFT IS RIGHT, OBEY THEM. ({SP_(154, 5, "אפילו", "מראים", "בעיניך", "על", "ימין", "שהוא", "שמאל")} "even if they show before your eyes that right is left"; {SP_(154, 5, "שמע", "להם")} "obey them"): THE COURT\'S RULING BINDS AGAINST THE EYE — the spelling here defective (17:11 with 5:32, asserted): the compile\'s obedience unconditioned on the subject\'s own judgment. Fresh.')
srow(155, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THE MAN WHO ACTS PRESUMPTUOUSLY" (17:12) — WHO DID NOT HEAR FROM THE MOUTH OF THE COURT AND TEACHES. The head row of piska 155 ({SP_(155, 1, "אשר", "לא", "שמע", "מפי", "בית", "דין", "ומורה")} "who did not hear from the mouth of the court and teaches"): THE REBEL ELDER — one who rules against the court he has not heeded (Sanhedrin 11:2): the compile\'s subject a teacher, not a litigant. Fresh.')
srow(155, 2, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHO ACTS" — FOR A DEED HE IS LIABLE, NOT FOR A RULING. ({SP_(155, 2, "על", "מעשה", "הוא", "חיב")} "for a deed he is liable"; {SP_(155, 2, "ואינו", "חיב", "על", "הוריה")} "and he is not liable for a ruling"): the liability on the ACT following the contrary ruling (the row without a citation) — the compile\'s trigger an act, the teaching alone no crime. Fresh.')
srow(155, 3, 'MATERIAL', f'"PRESUMPTUOUSLY" — FOR PRESUMPTION HE IS LIABLE, NOT FOR ERROR. ({SP_(155, 3, "על", "זדון", "הוא", "חיב", "ואינו", "חיב", "על", "שגגה")} "for presumption he is liable and he is not liable for error"): the intent condition — "presumptuously" the noun at 17:12 and 18:22 alone in the Torah (asserted): the rebel and the false prophet share the word and the condition (178:2). Fresh.')
srow(155, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"NOT TO HEARKEN" — AND NOT ONE WHO HEARS FROM THE MOUTH OF ONE WHO HEARD. ({SP_(155, 4, "ולא", "שומע", "מפי", "שומע")} "and not one who hears from the mouth of one who heard"): the ruling must reach him from the court itself, not at second hand — a provenance condition on the compile\'s ruling value. Fresh.')
srow(155, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'"TO THE PRIEST WHO STANDS TO MINISTER" — TEACHES THAT SERVICE IS VALID ONLY STANDING; IF HE SAT AND SERVED, HIS SERVICE IS INVALID. ({SP_(155, 5, "שאין", "שרות", "כשר", "אלא", "מעומד")} "that service is valid only standing"; {SP_(155, 5, "הא", "אם", "ישב", "ועבד", "עבודתו", "פסולה")} "if he sat and served his service is invalid"): the priest\'s STANDING a condition of valid service (Sifrei Numbers 39; 167:1 the twin at 18:5; 169:1 the sitting priest) — the compile\'s service cell with a posture parameter. Fresh.')
srow(155, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"OR TO THE JUDGE" — AS WE SAID: EVEN WITHOUT PRIESTS AND LEVITES IT IS VALID. ({SP_(155, 6, "זהו", "שאמרנו")} "this is what we said"): 153:3 repeated at the rebel\'s verse — the court valid without its priests. Fresh.')
srow(155, 7, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND THAT MAN SHALL DIE" — AN UNSPECIFIED DEATH SAID IN THE TORAH IS STRANGULATION. ({SP_(155, 7, "בסתם", "מיתה", "האמורה", "בתורה", "בחנק")} "an unspecified death said in the Torah — by strangulation"): THE DEFAULT DEATH strangulation (Mekhilta Nezikin 5; 178:1 the same rule for the false prophet) — the compile\'s execution mode parameter with a default. Fresh.')
srow(155, 8, 'MATERIAL', f'"THAT MAN" — NOT THE COERCED, NOT THE UNWITTING, NOT THE MISLED. ({SP_(155, 8, "לא", "אנוס", "ולא", "שוגג", "ולא", "מטעה")} "not the coerced, and not the unwitting, and not the misled"): 149:5\'s three exclusions on the rebel — the same pronoun, the same three conditions. Fresh.')
srow(155, 9, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SHALL PURGE THE EVIL FROM ISRAEL" — PURGE THE DOERS OF EVIL FROM ISRAEL. ({SP_(155, 9, "בער", "עושי", "הרעות", "מישראל")} "purge the doers of evil from Israel"): the formula\'s second form ("from Israel" — two seats, here and 22:22, asserted) read as at 151:3: persons removed. Fresh.')
srow(156, 1, 'MATERIAL', f'"WHEN YOU COME INTO THE LAND" (17:14) — DO THE COMMANDMENT SAID IN THE MATTER, FOR BY ITS REWARD YOU ENTER THE LAND. The head row of piska 156 ({SP_(156, 1, "עשה", "מצוה", "האמורה", "בענין")} "do the commandment said in the matter"; {SP_(156, 1, "שבשכרה", "תכנס", "לארץ")} "for by its reward you enter the land"): THE ENTRY FORMULA (17:14 shares ten tokens in order with 26:1, asserted) read as a condition — the king\'s law among the commandments the entry rewards (160:1, 162:3, 170:1, 174:1 the same trope): the compile\'s conditional on the entry. Fresh.')
srow(156, 2, 'CONTEXT', f'"WHICH THE LORD YOUR GOD GIVES YOU" — BY YOUR MERIT. ({SP_(156, 2, "בזכותך")} "by your merit"): the gift\'s reason. Fresh.')
srow(156, 3, 'CONTEXT', f'"AND POSSESS IT AND DWELL IN IT" — BY THE REWARD OF POSSESSING YOU DWELL. ({SP_(156, 3, "בשכר", "שתירש", "תשב")} "by the reward that you possess, you dwell"): the two verbs a sequence of rewards. Fresh.')
srow(156, 4, 'MATERIAL', f'"AND YOU SAY, I WILL SET A KING OVER ME" — R. NEHORAI: THIS IS A DISGRACE FOR ISRAEL, AS IT IS SAID "FOR THEY HAVE NOT REJECTED YOU BUT ME, FROM REIGNING OVER THEM" (1 SAMUEL 8:7). ({SP_(156, 4, "הרי", "זה", "דבר", "גני", "לישראל")} "this is a matter of disgrace for Israel"): THE KING A DISGRACE by Samuel\'s verse (the run\'s case, never read ahead; Tosefta Sanhedrin 4:5) — the request the people\'s word (17:14\'s first person "I will set", asserted): the compile\'s king a conditional the people trigger, not a command they receive. Fresh.')
srow(156, 5, 'MATERIAL', f'R. JUDAH: IS IT NOT A COMMANDMENT OF THE TORAH TO ASK A KING, AS IT IS SAID "SET, YOU SHALL SET A KING OVER YOU" (17:15)? WHY WERE THEY PUNISHED IN SAMUEL\'S DAYS? BECAUSE THEY ASKED TOO SOON. ({SP_(156, 5, "והלא", "מצוה", "מן", "התורה", "לשאול", "להם", "מלך")} "is it not a commandment from the Torah to ask a king for them"; {SP_(156, 5, "לפי", "שהקדימו", "על", "ידם")} "because they hastened it"): THE KING A COMMANDMENT (the infinitive absolute "set, you shall set", asserted) and the punishment for the TIMING — the dispute between R. Nehorai and R. Judah the compile\'s two arms (Sanhedrin 20b the segment if a cell needs it): the king\'s law a commandment with a clock. Fresh.')
srow(156, 6, 'MATERIAL', f'"LIKE ALL THE NATIONS AROUND ME" — R. NEHORAI: THEY ASKED A KING ONLY TO SERVE IDOLS, AS IT IS SAID "WE TOO SHALL BE LIKE ALL THE NATIONS, OUR KING SHALL JUDGE US AND GO OUT BEFORE US AND FIGHT OUR WARS" (1 SAMUEL 8:20). ({SP_(156, 6, "לא", "בקשו", "להם", "מלך", "אלא", "להעבידם", "עבודה", "זרה")} "they asked a king only to make them serve foreign worship"): "like all the nations" the fault\'s seat — one seat in the Bible (asserted); Samuel\'s elders end with 17:14\'s own two words (asserted): the compile\'s king cell distinguishes the commanded king from the nations\' — a purpose parameter. Fresh.')
